/**
\page peano_utilities Utilities

## d-dimensional loops

Peano builds every core library for two and three spatial dimensions. The build system sets the
preprocessor macro `DIMENSIONS` per target from the CMake `DIMENSION` keyword. The macro selects the
dimension at compile time. The cache variable `SUPPORTED_DIMENSIONS` lists the dimensions of a
build.

The header `peano4/Loop.h` offers the d-dimensional loops:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
peano4::dForEach(20, [&](const tarch::la::Vector<DIMENSIONS, int>& k) {
  // k is the d-dimensional index of the current entry of the 20^d patch.
  const tarch::la::Vector<DIMENSIONS, double> somePosition =
    offset + tarch::la::convertScalar<double>(k) * h;
  [...]
});
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

peano4::dForEach also takes a vector of per-axis ranges. peano4::dForEachCorner visits the 2^d
corners of a cube together with their linearised index. Both are constexpr functions. They run in
the execution space of their caller. Host code passes host lambdas. A kernel passes device
lambdas.

peano4::dLinearised() converts a d-dimensional index into one integer. peano4::dDelinearised()
converts the integer back. peano4::dLinearisedExclusive() and peano4::dDelinearisedExclusive() do
the same for the indices of a face. These indices skip one dimension.
*/
